\image{conf-umn-twtacs.jpg}

\p{\strong{Caption.} \strong{Traveling-wave tACS (twtACS)} — externally-imposed transcranial alternating fields that generate directional traveling waves across cortex. Human \strong{ECoG} confirmed the fields shift the phase/timing of multi-unit activity, and the induced waves produced direction- and speed-dependent effects on memory and visual-attention tasks — causal evidence that traveling-wave structure shapes cognition, not just correlates with it (PNAS 2026).}
